# Finite-dimensionality of the space Ω(D)

Theorem statement: `AlgebraicCurve.omegaSpace_finite_of_genusReached`
(`d286f11c-bbba-5dce-8654-5a8dd94c63db`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `4215658d-98da-5ea8-a71f-c932aa8e1714`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $K \subseteq F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra satisfying `IsCurveOver K F`, that is: every
nonzero $f \in F$ has a principal divisor of degree $0$, each place $v$ of $F/K$ has residue field
finite over $K$, and the module of Kähler differentials $\Omega[F/K]$ is free of rank one over $F$.
Assume further that the set `Place K F` of places is nonempty and that $L(0) = \{f \in F : v(f) \le
1 \text{ for all } v\}$, the Riemann–Roch space of the zero divisor, is finite-dimensional over $K$.
Let $\gamma$ be an integer and $D_0$ a divisor (a finitely supported function from places to
$\mathbb{Z}$) for which `RiemannGenusReachedAt γ D₀` holds, i.e. $L(D_0)$ is finite-dimensional over
$K$, $\deg D_0 - \mathrm{ell}(D_0) = \gamma - 1$, and $\deg D - \mathrm{ell}(D) \le \gamma - 1$ for
every divisor $D$, where $\deg$ is the additive extension of $v \mapsto \deg v$ and `ell` the
dimension invariant of the Riemann–Roch spaces. Then for every divisor $D$ the space `omegaSpace D`,
consisting of those $K$-linear functionals on the adele space $\bigsqcup_E$ `adeleBdd E` $\subseteq
(\mathrm{Place}\,K\,F \to F)$ that annihilate the submodule generated by `adeleBdd D` together with
`globalSub K F`, is a finite-dimensional $K$-vector space.

This is the finiteness of the space of Weil differentials bounded by a divisor $D$, dual to the
finiteness of the adelic cohomology $H^1(D)$ in the adelic (repartition) approach to the
Riemann–Roch theorem. It serves as the finiteness side condition in
[`AlgebraicCurve.exists_indexOfSpecialty_nsmul_single_eq_zero_of_genusReached`]
(thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.exists_indexOfSpecialty_nsmul_single_eq_zero_of_genusReached),
where the rank-one property of the space of differentials is established.

